WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: zh

00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:05.166
Hello, everyone. I'm Miss Wei Wei

00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:06.799
Graduated from the Central Academy of Fine Arts

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.666
I have been teaching painting for seven or eight years

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.866
I have been learning to paint for almost 30 years

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.266
I am a person who likes doing painting teaching very much

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.766
I enjoy teaching the students

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:17.899
The feeling that makes them realize something

00:00:17.966 --> 00:00:19.133
And this class

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.900
It's the one I have for all the little whites

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.500
Introduction to Beginners

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.500
He fits in with the full white

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.166
I've never studied painting before

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.666
Or in a real sense

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:31.733
People who feel very handicapped

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.666
This is the baby-sitter course for you

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.866
The purpose of this course

00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:37.899
I want you to get the hang of it

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.500
Draw some nice lines

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.266
I've thought about it many times

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.466
What is the most important basic ability for drawing

00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:45.266
In a very practical sense

00:00:45.266 --> 00:00:46.333
I think it's a line draft

00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:49.299
To sketch and color you need a line draft first

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:51.566
To paint watercolor, you need a line draft first

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.066
With the line draft you have everything that follows

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.200
For Xiao Bai

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.366
Line draft is a very cost-effective thing

00:00:57.366 --> 00:00:59.766
From the development of the whole sketch logic

00:00:59.966 --> 00:01:02.866
Sketch is indeed from the line draft began to develop

00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:03.866
Only in the Soviet Union

00:01:03.866 --> 00:01:05.566
And then it slowly turned into this

00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:07.333
Full of color

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.066
It looks like a black and white photo

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.333
What about my class

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:12.199
I'm going to show you four pictures

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:15.166
Every operation is broken up and crumpled for you

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:16.133
It's very detailed

00:01:16.266 --> 00:01:17.099
Your last class

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.600
A partial line drawing of Menzel will be drawn

00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:20.199
I know that

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.500
There are a lot of little white hearts that create a kind of confusion

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:23.666
Really?

00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:25.166
Must be the

00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:27.333
Let's see if my teaching results are good

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.933
I teach a lot of students

00:01:29.066 --> 00:01:31.199
There are, like, ten thousand of them

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.533
From a 78-year-old kid to a man in his 70s

00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:36.099
Full age coverage

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.466
Full career coverage

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.166
There are a lot of other people

00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:42.266
In half a year or so you can draw the following

00:01:42.266 --> 00:01:43.366
A delicate portrait

00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:04.166
These results

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.799
Basically all 0 foundation small white learns

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.100
But in my heart

00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:10.266
There was always another goal that I wanted to challenge

00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:12.399
Because those were paying students

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.900
They set aside a time to learn it

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.566
The mentality is different when you pay

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.533
I always wish I could make a free course

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.900
Let a lot of small white wandering outside the door

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.566
Also experienced the fun of painting

00:02:23.866 --> 00:02:25.166
We've done some in the past

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:28.366
But this time I decided to do something more systematic

00:02:28.366 --> 00:02:31.599
I believe this course will make it easy for you

00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:34.099
Experience the whole technique of painting

00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:35.666
What about the method I used

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:38.133
It's a grid method from the Renaissance

00:02:38.266 --> 00:02:41.133
It is a method with replication as the main idea

00:02:41.366 --> 00:02:42.966
We'll start with the starting grid

00:02:42.966 --> 00:02:44.566
We only have 4 cells in the back

00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:45.766
In the process

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.900
Core exercise ability

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.133
The ability to see position and scale

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:50.966
This is actually a realistic painting

00:02:50.966 --> 00:02:52.799
Is a very important basic ability

00:02:52.866 --> 00:02:54.166
As long as you can judge correctly

00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:55.766
Where is every position in the picture

00:02:55.766 --> 00:02:57.066
What is the size ratio

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.333
I can draw it very well

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.266
This grid method

00:02:59.266 --> 00:03:01.466
In fact, the old masters used to teach themselves

00:03:01.466 --> 00:03:02.366
Apprentice painter

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.366
Rafi, Leonardo Da Vinci learned that

00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:06.933
The painters of that time

00:03:06.933 --> 00:03:08.066
In order to get his own apprentice

00:03:08.066 --> 00:03:09.499
Draw your manuscript quickly

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:11.366
It's usually taught this way

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:12.533
A lot of students

00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:14.966
It takes about a month to two months to get started

00:03:14.966 --> 00:03:16.566
But in this day and age

00:03:16.566 --> 00:03:17.933
I wish he could be faster

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.333
I don't know if people are starting to feel confident

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.533
So take this course

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:23.099
What do you need to prepare

00:03:23.166 --> 00:03:25.999
It's easy. I've got a workbook for you

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.333
The assignments for each lesson are in this workbook

00:03:28.466 --> 00:03:29.866
You need to go inside the print shop

00:03:29.866 --> 00:03:31.566
Print it out on A4 paper

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:34.966
The rest of the tools a pen and an eraser are enough

00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:37.166
There are no cool special effects throughout the course

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.500
There is no complicated production

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.500
But they cost us a lot of work

00:03:40.566 --> 00:03:41.933
As we make the course

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:43.999
Record each drawing 7-8 times

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.299
The first time is to teach yourself

00:03:46.466 --> 00:03:48.533
The second time was to teach a colleague

00:03:48.766 --> 00:03:51.599
The third time is for some past students to experience

00:03:51.666 --> 00:03:54.099
Until you get to the real fallible part of the picture

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.533
When it's all distilled

00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:58.999
Do elaborate explanation in every specific detail

00:03:59.066 --> 00:04:00.933
This is a no-frills course

00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:02.533
There is only one core purpose

00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:04.133
I just hope you understand

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:04.933
Will learn

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.500
That's what I've been teaching for

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.666
If you're ready

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:11.299
So let's go on this trip together

00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:13.533
An introduction to painting learning

00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:16.099
I hope you get the confidence to paint

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.700
Formally enter the door of painting

